<Legal
  title="PoroScout - Privacy Policy"
  description="The Privacy Policy for PoroScout, the League of Legends Discord bot."
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  lastUpdated="2026-06-06"
>
  <section>
    <h2>Data Collection</h2>
    <p>PoroScout collects the following information:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Your <strong>Discord account ID</strong> and your
        <strong>League of Legends username, region, and ID</strong>
        (when using the <code>/link</code> command).
      </li>
      <li>Anonymous website and bot usage data.</li>
      <li>
        In the event the bot malfunctions when a command gets invoked, the error
        along with context information will be sent over to
        <a href="https://sentry.io">Sentry.io</a> to be analyzed.
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Data includes the following:</strong></li>
          <li>User, Guild, and Channel ID</li>
          <li>Command Name</li>
          <li>Command Options if applicable</li>
          <li>Error details</li>
        </ul>
      </li>
      <li>
        If linked, daily statistics of the linked League account's LP, rank,
        division, and tier.
        <ul>
          <li>
            LP History data is <strong>not</strong> directly linked to your Discord
            account, instead it is linked to your League account's PUUID.
          </li>
          <li>
            This means, in the unlikely event that our LP history database gets
            breached, there is no way to draw a line between your Discord and
            League account.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </li>
      <li>
        Your League of Legends account data (rank, past matches, profile, etc.)
        is stored but is not directly linked to your Discord account.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      Throughout this page, you will see the term:
      <i>personally identifying information</i>
      (<a href="https://www.dol.gov/general/ppii">PII</a>) used. In the case of
      the bot, data that is PII is data that can link directly to your Discord
      account's ID, which includes your linked League of Legends account name
      and region.
    </p>

    <p>
      PoroScout will never share any personally identifying information publicly
      without your consent unless required by law, unless otherwise stated in
      this document. To unlink your League of Legends username, region, and ID
      from your Discord account, you can run <code>/unlink</code>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Data Retention</h2>
    <p>Different categories of data are retained for different periods:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Personally identifying information</strong> (the link between your
        Discord account and your League account) is retained for
        <strong>30 days</strong>, as per Discord's guidelines. It is
        automatically deleted 30 days after your last command was run (processed
        at midnight UTC). You may also delete it at any time by running
        <code>/unlink</code>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>LP history data</strong> (linked to your League account's PUUID, not
        your Discord account) is retained
        <strong>indefinitely</strong> to provide long-term statistics and graphs.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>General League of Legends account data</strong> (rank, past matches,
        profile, etc.) is cached and retained for as long as the cache remains valid.
        This data is not linked to your Discord account.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Third-Party Services</h2>
    <p>
      PoroScout relies on a number of third-party services to operate. Your
      <strong>Discord account ID is never shared with any third party</strong>,
      with the sole exception of error reporting (see below). When data is sent
      to a third party for League of Legends features, the most that is ever
      shared are the command options you provide (such as a Riot username or a
      champion name), and this data is not linked to your Discord account.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong><a href="https://sentry.io">Sentry</a></strong>: error
        reporting. This is the only third party that may receive data linked to
        your Discord account, and only when a command fails (see the Data
        Collection section above).
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong><a href="https://www.netlify.com">Netlify</a></strong>: hosts
        this website. The website is served from Netlify's global network.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong><a href="https://www.cloudflare.com">Cloudflare</a></strong>:
        acts as a proxy in front of our infrastructure.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong><a href="https://plausible.io">Plausible Analytics</a></strong>
        : self-hosted, privacy-friendly, cookieless website analytics. See the Website
        Analytics section below.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong
          ><a href="https://developer.riotgames.com">Riot Games API</a></strong
        >: source of League of Legends account and match data. Queries are not
        linked to your Discord account.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong><a href="https://mobalytics.gg">Mobalytics</a></strong>: source
        of additional League of Legends data. Requests are not linked to your
        Discord account.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong
          ><a href="https://www.communitydragon.org/">CommunityDragon</a
          ></strong
        >: source of League of Legends game assets and data. Requests are not
        linked to your Discord account.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Our bot/website may contain links to third-party websites that are not
      operated by us. We have no control over and assume no responsibility for
      the content, privacy policies, or practices of any third-party sites or
      services.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Website Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      We use <a href="https://plausible.io">Plausible Analytics</a>, hosted on
      our own infrastructure, to collect anonymous website usage data. Plausible
      does not use cookies and does not collect any personally identifying
      information. Website analytics are not associated with your Discord
      account.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Bot Usage Data</h2>
    <p>
      We collect anonymous data about how the bot's commands are used. Where
      this usage data is associated with a Discord account ID, that ID is
      <strong>hashed</strong> before storage so that it cannot be reversed. However,
      given a known Discord account ID, the corresponding hashed usage data can still
      be correlated back to that account.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Data Security</h2>
    <p>
      Your data is stored on our own bare-metal infrastructure. Stored data
      <i>that is personally identifying</i> is <strong>encrypted</strong> for added
      protection. While we take reasonable measures to protect your data, no method
      of transmission or storage is completely secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute
      security.
    </p>
    <p>
      In the unlikely event of a data breach, we will post a notification in our
      Discord server describing the extent of the breach as soon as we are
      reasonably able to, and in any case within 72 hours of becoming aware of
      it. Because PoroScout does not collect email addresses, our Discord server
      and this website are the only channels through which we can notify you.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Your Privacy Rights</h2>
    <p>
      Depending on where you live, you may have rights over your personal data
      under laws such as the EU/UK General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) and
      the California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA). These may include the right
      to:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Access the personal data we hold about you.</li>
      <li>Request correction of inaccurate data.</li>
      <li>Request deletion of your data.</li>
      <li>Request a copy of your data in a portable format.</li>
      <li>Object to or restrict certain processing of your data.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      You can exercise your right to deletion at any time by running
      <code>/unlink</code>, which removes the link between your Discord and
      League accounts. For any other request, or to delete other data we may
      hold, contact us using the email in the Questions section below. We do not
      <strong>sell</strong> your personal data to anyone.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      PoroScout is not directed at children under the age of 13, and we do not
      knowingly collect personal data from anyone under 13. If you believe that
      a child under 13 has provided us with personal data, please contact us and
      we will delete it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>International Users</h2>
    <p>
      PoroScout's application and database are hosted on bare-metal
      infrastructure located in Charlotte, North Carolina, United States. This
      website is served globally through Netlify. If you access PoroScout from
      outside the United States, you understand that your data will be
      transferred to, stored, and processed in the United States. By using the
      bot, you consent to this transfer.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. The "Last updated"
      date at the top of this page reflects the most recent revision. Material
      changes will be announced in our Discord server. Your continued use of the
      bot after any changes take effect constitutes your acceptance of the
      revised policy.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Affiliation</h2>
    <p>
      PoroScout isn't endorsed by Riot Games and doesn't reflect the views or
      opinions of Riot Games or anyone officially involved in producing or
      managing Riot Games properties. Riot Games, and all associated properties
      are trademarks or registered trademarks of Riot Games, Inc.
    </p>
    <p>
      PoroScout is also not affiliated with Discord. Discord is a registered
      trademark of Discord, Inc. Any direct connection to Discord and/or its
      trademark is purely coincidental. We do not claim to have any copyright
      ownership of Discord and/or its assets.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>
      Have any questions? Feel free to email me at
      <EmailLink user="derock" domain="derock.dev" />.
    </p>
  </section>
</Legal>
